# /production-implement — Stage 5 Production Implementation

**IRON LAW:** Code may be changed only after the Project Contract and Stage-4 plan pass preflight. Working UI or passing unit tests alone never establishes completion.

Stage 5 requires an **approved, current Project Contract** and an approved Stage-4 plan. Revalidate authoritative source hashes, blocking conflicts, pending human gates, branch safety, scope, all 75 control decisions, required tests, evidence, rollback and recovery before implementation proceeds.

All 75 deterministic baseline controls must be classified for the implementation slice. Every applicable control must have a gate, a passing test and evidence. Escalate remains blocking until a human technical decision; Forbidden rejects the implementation path.

After successful Stage-5 verification, hand off to `/review`. Stage 5 may emit `IMPLEMENTATION COMPLETE` or `BLOCKED`; it must never declare `PRODUCTION APPROVED` or bypass independent review, QA, ship, deployment or canary stages.

Canonical external pipeline remains Stage 0 `/project-init`, 1 `/office-hours`, 2 `/plan-ceo-review`, 3 `/plan-eng-review`, 4 `/autoplan`, 5 `/production-implement`, 6 `/review`, 7 `/qa`, 8 `/ship`, 9 `/land-and-deploy`, 10 `/canary`. PREOS engines are internal intelligence, not extra mandatory stages.

